{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace","id":1557832,"title":"Questions on the Mouth of Peace","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-22T07:59:15-08:00","id":1557832,"title":"Questions on the Mouth of Peace","content":"Hi, so what are the qualities the order looks for in the &quot;reincarnation&quot; of the mouth of peace? Do they have any political considerations, like trying to avoid dynasts in favor of outcastes or the opposite? If the Mouth is from a DB house does the Order try to curtail the house's influence on her? If the child fails to exalt and is deemed not the Mouth, what happens to the kid then? Kicked out of the order? Is the Mouth trained any different from other DB's who join the faith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T12:35:11-08:00","id":1557838,"title":"","content":"Page 91 of The Realm gives us extremely loose guidelines, favoring nebulous &quot;spiritual criteria&quot; and passing &quot;specially designed tests,&quot; as well as the much more specific and perhaps informative pieces, &quot;with Sidereal guidance&quot; and &quot;likely to Exalt.&quot; This is leaving a lot on the table for STs, but it gives us a basic framework to piece things together.<br /> <br /> &quot;Likely to Exalt&quot; is a strong indicator towards the Dynasty; even if the process theoretically isn't supposed to be influenced by political connections, in practice I imagine there'll be a lot of jockeying among the Great Houses to get their daughters shots at those special tests, especially among the Houses with reputations for piety.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting, though, because the age guideline given for settling on a candidate is &quot;before she's 15 years old,&quot; which, while on the younger side in general, isn't <i>so</i> young that you couldn't just pick from among the plausible candidates who've <i>already</i> Exalted. Maybe there's supposed to be something of cultural significance to finding the new Mouth before she Exalts, something that sells the selection process as special in a way that validates to the public the claims that they're finding the same soul over and over? In which case we flip back to the Dalai Lama parallel and it becomes way better to pick an outcaste. <i>If</i> they can predict an outcaste's Exaltation with any degree of consistency with enough behind-the-scenes genealogical tracking and Sidereal prophecy/shenanigans, that would make the choice both a lot more House-neutral <i>and</i> lend more miraculous credence to the Mouth of Peace having a detectable special quality.<br /> <br /> (Though on the flip side - a young outcaste who chooses the razor is already someone the Order has direct access to and is training potentially well before a Dynast would enter secondary school, so if there <i>isn't</i> a special reason to find girls <i>before</i> they Exalt, that could still work to an outcaste's advantage in potentially being selected.)<br /> <br /> Speaking of Sidereal oversight, we can probably guess from that that long-term outcomes are gonna be factored more than the House politicking, even if that gets girls in the door.<br /> <br /> I would assume that the Mouth of Peace gets special training and attention relative to everyone else in the Order for her specific role, though maybe after going through the basics with everyone else just to instill a sense of humility and cohesion.<br /> <br /> I suspect that wrongly-selected Mouths wouldn't be formally kicked out - it was the selectors who messed up, not them - but in practice, they probably have their public presence circumscribed and are more likely to develop a spontaneous case of dead, because it's almost unavoidable that a certain number of people will have grown attached to the first person declared the Mouth of Peace and be resistant to the establishment later going &quot;oopsy, here's the real one instead&quot; and that's a mighty recipe for factional infighting and a splinter sect right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T03:18:42-08:00","id":1557851,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think that the premise of &quot;a failed Mouth of Peace is marked for death&quot; trends a little too grimdark. If nothing else, it seems patently unnecessary; it's a system primed for the supremacy of Dragon-Blooded, and even assuming that there was any basis for the monks to become attached to some pre-teen girl in the first place sufficient to threaten a schism, I should imagine there are numerous practical steps that can be enacted to isolate them.<br /> <br /> I think the benefit of Sidereals would largely be a matter of being able to quickly hone in on folks with the correct criteria and good bloodlines; as I recall, Exaltation itself remains beyond the sight of pretty much any prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T08:50:23-08:00","id":1557858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557838#post1557838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 91 of The Realm gives us extremely loose guidelines, favoring nebulous &quot;spiritual criteria&quot; and passing &quot;specially designed tests,&quot; as well as the much more specific and perhaps informative pieces, &quot;with Sidereal guidance&quot; and &quot;likely to Exalt.&quot; This is leaving a lot on the table for STs, but it gives us a basic framework to piece things together.<br /> <br /> &quot;Likely to Exalt&quot; is a strong indicator towards the Dynasty; even if the process theoretically isn't supposed to be influenced by political connections, in practice I imagine there'll be a lot of jockeying among the Great Houses to get their daughters shots at those special tests, especially among the Houses with reputations for piety. <br /> <br /> <br /> It's also interesting, though, because the age guideline given for settling on a candidate is &quot;before she's 15 years old,&quot; which, while on the younger side in general, isn't <i>so</i> young that you couldn't just pick from among the plausible candidates who've <i>already</i> Exalted. Maybe there's supposed to be something of cultural significance to finding the new Mouth before she Exalts, something that sells the selection process as special in a way that validates to the public the claims that they're finding the same soul over and over? In which case we flip back to the Dalai Lama parallel and it becomes way better to pick an outcaste. <i>If</i> they can predict an outcaste's Exaltation with any degree of consistency with enough behind-the-scenes genealogical tracking and Sidereal prophecy/shenanigans, that would make the choice both a lot more House-neutral <i>and</i> lend more miraculous credence to the Mouth of Peace having a detectable special quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. If it's important to find someone who hasn't already exalted, then it gives a degree of separation from the Dynasts and doesn't become the medieval era of popes bribing their way to power using their families' money. Even if there is probably a higher chance of the Mouth coming from a Dynast family. Keeping to the Dalai Lama parallel I'm kinda surprised there isn't a Panchen Lama equiavlent who is supposed to look for the Mouth and the Mouth for them when they reincarnate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557838#post1557838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Though on the flip side - a young outcaste who chooses the razor is already someone the Order has direct access to and is training potentially well before a Dynast would enter secondary school, so if there <i>isn't</i> a special reason to find girls <i>before</i> they Exalt, that could still work to an outcaste's advantage in potentially being selected.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like it be the &quot;safest&quot; backup option if that makes sense. You've got a pious monk already with the right powers and potentially years to groom and shape her to be the best possible Mouth<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557838#post1557838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume that the Mouth of Peace gets special training and attention relative to everyone else in the Order for her specific role, though maybe after going through the basics with everyone else just to instill a sense of humility and cohesion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, probably the cloister of wisdom with more private instruction and some advisors? And probably some Siderals making sure there aren't any assassins? <br /> <br /> Do we know if the Mouth is allowed or Dynasts try to keep contact with their old families or would it be discouraged both for their role and to make sure DB houses aren't in control of things? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T09:41:26-08:00","id":1557859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557858#post1557858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that. If it's important to find someone who hasn't already exalted, then it gives a degree of separation from the Dynasts and doesn't become the medieval era of popes bribing their way to power using their families' money.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those areas where I feel as though the presence of Exalted lends a certain robustness to institutions that might not be present in reality. Like, I think the general presentation of the Immaculate Order is such that the faith of the upper echelons is fairly genuine, and they're pretty resistant on both a systemic and personal level against corruption.<br /> <br /> And one could look at that in relation to things like Integrity Charms and how much that empowers people to hold fast to their principles in the face of temptations.<br /> <br /> It helps that the Immaculate Order is older than the Scarlet Dynasty and has some degree of investment in remaining an independent institution from them. Dynasts may be where the many if not most of their Exalted are coming from, but that doesn't mean they need to be beholden to the interests of the Great Houses.<br /> <br /> It probably helps that Mnemon is probably the House most closely associated with the Order, and Mnemon herself is a true believer with a debt of gratitude towards them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T10:46:24-08:00","id":1557861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557851#post1557851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think that the premise of &quot;a failed Mouth of Peace is marked for death&quot; trends a little too grimdark. If nothing else, it seems patently unnecessary; it's a system primed for the supremacy of Dragon-Blooded, and even assuming that there was any basis for the monks to become attached to some pre-teen girl in the first place sufficient to threaten a schism, I should imagine there are numerous practical steps that can be enacted to isolate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off - she's not &quot;some pre-teen&quot; for long. They select a Mouth young, prior to 15 and prior to Exaltation, but if she's a didn't-Exalt failure case they're not gonna know that for sure til she's over 20, so that's several years in the role to build connections.<br /> <br /> But I wasn't even really talking about the monks; the Mouth of Peace is an extremely public-facing role. Her job description is basically &quot;inspire the faithful masses + personify and represent them in the halls of power.&quot; She is not a figure whose relevance is limited primarily to the monks she works with day to day.<br /> <br /> Particularly if the two young women make differing impressions on the public, something in particular for a group of people to feel like they're losing in the transition in terms of being understood, or a leaning on a given political stance... But honestly even without all that, I think it's just a factor of human nature that a certain number of people will have grown invested in the first thing they heard and suspicious about take-backsies. And on an even wider level than any emotional investment in the first Mouth, the simple fact of the Order having just publicly gotten it wrong is going to create complications for the newly-selected Mouth in establishing her legitimacy to the public.<br /> <br /> I don't think it would be an easily brushed over moment in the religious history of Immaculacy, and, to bring this back to the monks, a good time for any with a movement in mind or who want to swing a higher position in a smaller group over their current status to throw themselves behind a public splinter.<br /> <br /> ... Mind you, I don't want to exaggerate this; I don't think assassination is a first or common way to deal with the occasional wrong-Mouth. Not only is assassination kind of frowned on in general, it's also fuel to the fire for any sentiments against a new Mouth. No, I think mostly it's dealt with by making sure the wrong-Mouth stops going outside and talking to people for a while until her supporters mostly get over it and get with the program. But <i>if</i> she tries to maintain her position of public prominence (which, with or without claiming to be the real Mouth after all, would certainly keep such sentiments alive), that's where elevated risk of death starts setting in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T12:47:10-08:00","id":1557864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557861#post1557861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off - she's not &quot;some pre-teen&quot; for long. They select a Mouth young, prior to 15 and prior to Exaltation, but if she's a didn't-Exalt failure case they're not gonna know that for sure til she's over 20, so that's several years in the role to build connections.<br /> <br /> But I wasn't even really talking about the monks; the Mouth of Peace is an extremely public-facing role. Her job description is basically &quot;inspire the faithful masses + personify and represent them in the halls of power.&quot; She is not a figure whose relevance is limited primarily to the monks she works with day to day.<br /> <br /> Particularly if the two young women make differing impressions on the public, something in particular for a group of people to feel like they're losing in the transition in terms of being understood, or a leaning on a given political stance... But honestly even without all that, I think it's just a factor of human nature that a certain number of people will have grown invested in the first thing they heard and suspicious about take-backsies. And on an even wider level than any emotional investment in the first Mouth, the simple fact of the Order having just publicly gotten it wrong is going to create complications for the newly-selected Mouth in establishing her legitimacy to the public.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is giving neither the Sidereals nor the Order very much credit to say that they don't keep their candidates out of the public sphere before they can be locked in by the act of Exalting.<br /> <br /> Certainly, being unExalted means they lack the proper standing to exert any kind of spiritual authority at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T14:09:33-08:00","id":1557867,"title":"","content":"They also probably don't let the kid immeditately start handing out decrees and making policy changes until they are older if I had to guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T14:49:03-08:00","id":1557869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557864#post1557864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is giving neither the Sidereals nor the Order very much credit to say that they don't keep their candidates out of the public sphere before they can be locked in by the act of Exalting.<br /> <br /> Certainly, being unExalted means they lack the proper standing to exert any kind of spiritual authority at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I gave them an appropriate amount of credit, in a way that aligns with what's written in the book. If they don't have a particular reason to stake a claim on a candidate before they Exalt, the smart - and blindingly obvious - thing to do is to just pick from among young Exalts, but they're unambiguously written as tending to settle on their choice prior to Exaltation, with a whole blurb about them going into overtime to find the &quot;true&quot; reincarnation quickly if their candidate doesn't Exalt. Hence my postulating on the myth-legitimizing cultural impact of revealing them before they Exalt as proof to those outside the search effort that they <i>really can </i>find the same special soul over and over, especially if the things that make them likely to Exalt aren't public knowledge (i.e. if they don't come directly from the Dynasty). It's also written that this almost always works out for the selectors, and I figured the occasional exceptions were written in for basically the exact ST utility I'm ascribing to them (for example, being able to originate an Immaculate heresy in a group who stuck by a retracted Mouth of Peace and went underground or fled to the Threshold or whatever).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557867#post1557867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also probably don't let the kid immeditately start handing out decrees and making policy changes until they are older if I had to guess.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Mouth of Peace also doesn't really handle decrees or policy. Again, her role is &quot;inspiring voice for the people&quot; and &quot;voice for the voiceless.&quot; She has enough sheer religious standing that many are successful at leveraging it into political sway, but the same sidebar on p. 91 of The Realm points out that political power is <i>not</i> inherent to the job.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","user":"MJ6373","date":".  Responding to a post made after I started writing mine 01-23-2026, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T15:57:37-08:00","id":1557870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557869#post1557869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't have a particular reason to stake a claim on a candidate before they Exalt, the smart - and blindingly obvious - thing to do is to just pick from among young Exalts, but they're unambiguously written as tending to settle on their choice prior to Exaltation, with a whole blurb about them going into overtime to find the &quot;true&quot; reincarnation quickly if their candidate doesn't Exalt. Hence my postulating on the myth-legitimizing cultural impact of revealing them before they Exalt as proof to those outside the search effort that they <i>really can </i>find the same special soul over and over, especially if the things that make them likely to Exalt aren't public knowledge (i.e. if they don't come directly from the Dynasty).</div> </div> </div> </div>The mythology of the Immaculate Order is that Dragon-Blooded are reincarnated from enlightened souls who have proven their worth in the Perfected Hierarchy over multiple lifetimes. By definition, <i>every</i> Exalt in the Scarlet Dynasty is a special soul. The Mouth of Peace is exceptional, but not in a sense that needs to act as though reincarnation is randomized.<br /> <br /> I think the primary reason to choose a Mouth before they Exalt is to validate the idea that Exaltation comes to such worthy souls, and that the Mouth is Immaculate to a point that they can be recognized ahead of time in a way that no other reincarnation can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also written that this almost always works out for the selectors, and I figured the occasional exceptions were written in for basically the exact ST utility I'm ascribing to them (for example, being able to originate an Immaculate heresy in a group who stuck by a retracted Mouth of Peace and went underground or fled to the Threshold or whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure that the occasional exceptions are written in to give the Sidereals a contingency to maintain the facade in spite of the fact that they can't actually predict who will Exalt with one hundred percent certainty.<br /> <br /> A person can develop their own idea of a heresy that formed around a wrong pick for Mouth of Peace, but that's an exception within an exception, not an existential threat so intrinsic that it's necessary to murder every mortal selection lest the Order fragment over and over.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T18:34:17-08:00","id":1557871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557832-questions-on-the-mouth-of-peace?p=1557870#post1557870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mythology of the Immaculate Order is that Dragon-Blooded are reincarnated from enlightened souls who have proven their worth in the Perfected Hierarchy over multiple lifetimes. By definition, <i>every</i> Exalt in the Scarlet Dynasty is a special soul. The Mouth of Peace is exceptional, but not in a sense that needs to act as though reincarnation is randomized.<br /> <br /> I think the primary reason to choose a Mouth before they Exalt is to validate the idea that Exaltation comes to such worthy souls, and that the Mouth is Immaculate to a point that they can be recognized ahead of time in a way that no other reincarnation can be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I figure that the occasional exceptions are written in to give the Sidereals a contingency to maintain the facade in spite of the fact that they can't actually predict who will Exalt with one hundred percent certainty.<br /> <br /> A person can develop their own idea of a heresy that formed around a wrong pick for Mouth of Peace, but that's an exception within an exception, not an existential threat so intrinsic that it's necessary to murder every mortal selection lest the Order fragment over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I communicating really badly or something? I feel like I said to begin with and clarified again that the typical thing to do with a removed Mouth is just to circumscribe her public participation for a while until people have mostly forgotten about her. I hardly think it's a circumstance that would usually or expectedly result in assassination. It just <i>is</i> a situation that inherently complicates the legitimacy of whichever Mouth they pick next while leaving the original pick with a residual clout and legitimacy that won't disappear when the administration snaps their fingers, especially if she <i>tries</i> to maintain her public presence. Which <i>sometimes</i> creates incentives to violence to maintain political cohesion.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure how the other parts of your post are disagreeing with me. We seem to be on the same page that occasionally needing to find a new Mouth is a product of the clash between the myth of the Mouth's inherent spirituality making her detectable pre-Exaltation against the fact that Exaltation can't actually be perfectly predicted. From there, it's seemed like our disagreement has basically been about 1) how public the first Mouth's occupation of that position was (I argue it must be, or else the myth-making serves little to no purpose), and 2) how people respond to seeing the selection changed after several years because their first candidate didn't Exalt (which, consequent to the view that the first Mouth would be a known figure, is inclined to produce interesting consequences of contested legitimacy, running the gamut from the circumstances creating a small thorn in the new Mouth's side in establishing public acceptance and reverence, to the extreme end of the original pick shaping into an antipope figure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}